AC-01	Access Control	Quarterly logical access reviews are conducted for all critical systems to ensure least privilege.	IT Director	SOC 2 (CC6.3); ISO 27001 (A.9.2.5); HIPAA (164.308)	Needs Improvement	
AC-02	Access Control	Privileged access is restricted to authorized administrators and reviewed quarterly.	IT Director	SOC 2 (CC6.2); ISO 27001 (A.9.2.3); FedRAMP (AC-6)	Effective	
AC-03	Access Control	User accounts are disabled within 24 hours of employee termination.	IT Operations	SOC 2 (CC6.1); ISO 27001 (A.9.2.6); HIPAA (164.308)	Effective	
AC-04	Access Control	Multi-factor authentication (MFA) is required for all privileged and remote access accounts.	IT Operations	SOC 2 (CC6.6); ISO 27001 (A.9.4.2); FedRAMP (IA-2)	Effective	
IA-01	Identity & Authentication	Password complexity requirements are enforced through Microsoft Entra ID.	IT Operations	SOC 2 (CC6.1); ISO 27001 (A.9.4.3); PCI DSS (Req. 8)	Effective	
IA-02	Identity & Authentication	Single Sign-On (SSO) is implemented for corporate applications.	IT Operations	SOC 2 (CC6.2); ISO 27001 (A.9.4.2)	Effective	
IA-03	Identity & Authentication	Service accounts are inventoried and reviewed annually.	Infrastructure Team	SOC 2 (CC6.1); ISO 27001 (A.9.2.1)	Needs Improvement	
BC-01	Backup & Recovery	Automated backups of production databases are performed daily and tested monthly for restorability.	Cloud Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.3); ISO 27001 (A.12.3.1); HIPAA (164.308)	Effective	
BC-02	Backup & Recovery	Disaster Recovery plans are tested annually.	Cloud Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.4); ISO 27001 (A.17.1); FedRAMP (CP-4)	Needs Improvement	
BC-03	Backup & Recovery	Recovery Time Objectives (RTO) and Recovery Point Objectives (RPO) are documented and validated.	Cloud Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.4); ISO 27001 (A.17.1)	Effective	
VM-01	Vulnerability Management	Vulnerability scans are performed monthly on external-facing assets; critical vulnerabilities are remediated within seven days.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.1); PCI DSS (Req. 11); FedRAMP (RA-5)	Effective	
VM-02	Vulnerability Management	Internal authenticated vulnerability scans are performed monthly.	Security Operations	ISO 27001 (A.12.6.1); PCI DSS (Req. 11)	Effective	
VM-03	Vulnerability Management	Annual third-party penetration testing is conducted and tracked to remediation.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.1); ISO 27001 (A.18.2.3); PCI DSS (Req. 11.4)	Needs Improvement	
CM-01	Change Management	All production changes require documented approval prior to implementation.	Engineering Manager	SOC 2 (CC8.1); ISO 27001 (A.12.1.2)	Effective	
CM-02	Change Management	Emergency changes follow a documented emergency change process with retrospective approval.	Engineering Manager	SOC 2 (CC8.1); ISO 27001 (A.12.1.2)	Effective	
CM-03	Change Management	Infrastructure changes are tracked through ServiceNow.	IT Operations	SOC 2 (CC8.1); ISO 27001 (A.12.1.2)	Effective	
IR-01	Incident Response	Security incidents are documented and managed through the Incident Response Plan.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.4); ISO 27001 (A.16.1); HIPAA (164.308)	Effective	
IR-02	Incident Response	Incident response tabletop exercises are conducted annually.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.4); ISO 27001 (A.16.1.6); FedRAMP (IR-3)	Needs Improvement	
IR-03	Incident Response	Lessons learned are documented following significant security incidents.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.4); ISO 27001 (A.16.1.6)	Effective	
LM-01	Logging & Monitoring	Security logs are centrally collected and retained for at least one year.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.2); ISO 27001 (A.12.4.1); FedRAMP (AU-2)	Effective	
LM-02	Logging & Monitoring	SIEM alerts are monitored 24x7 for suspicious activity.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.2); ISO 27001 (A.12.4.3)	Effective	
LM-03	Logging & Monitoring	Privileged administrative actions are logged and reviewed.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC6.6); ISO 27001 (A.12.4.3); FedRAMP (AU-6)	Needs Improvement	
AM-01	Asset Management	An inventory of hardware, software, and cloud assets is maintained and reviewed quarterly.	IT Asset Manager	SOC 2 (CC1.2); ISO 27001 (A.8.1.1)	Effective	
AM-02	Asset Management	Data classification standards are applied to information assets.	Information Security	ISO 27001 (A.8.2); HIPAA (164.312)	Effective	
VR-01	Vendor Risk	Critical third-party vendors undergo annual security assessments.	Vendor Risk Manager	SOC 2 (CC9.2); ISO 27001 (A.15.1); FedRAMP (SA-9)	Effective	
VR-02	Vendor Risk	Vendor SOC reports and certifications are reviewed annually.	Vendor Risk Manager	SOC 2 (CC9.2); ISO 27001 (A.15.1)	Needs Improvement	
SA-01	Security Awareness	Annual security awareness training is completed by all employees.	HR & Security	SOC 2 (CC2.2); ISO 27001 (A.7.2.2); HIPAA (164.308)	Effective	
SA-02	Security Awareness	Quarterly phishing simulations are conducted to assess user awareness.	Security Operations	SOC 2 (CC2.2); ISO 27001 (A.7.2.2)	Effective	
BCP-01	Business Continuity	Business Continuity Plans are reviewed annually.	Business Continuity Manager	SOC 2 (CC7.4); ISO 27001 (A.17.1)	Needs Improvement	
BCP-02	Business Continuity	Critical business processes are supported by documented recovery procedures.	Business Continuity Manager	ISO 27001 (A.17.1); FedRAMP (CP-2)	Effective	
GP-01	Governance	Information Security Policies are reviewed and approved annually.	CISO	SOC 2 (CC1.1); ISO 27001 (A.5.1.1)	Effective	
GP-02	Governance	Annual enterprise risk assessments are performed.	GRC Manager	SOC 2 (CC3.2); ISO 27001 (Clause 6.1); NIST CSF	Effective	
GP-03	Governance	Customer security questionnaires are completed and tracked through a centralized process.	GRC Team	SOC 2 (CC9.2); ISO 27001 (A.15); HIPAA	Needs Improvement	
CR-01	Cyber Resilience	Backup recovery exercises are performed quarterly to validate ransomware recovery procedures and recovery objectives (RTO/RPO).	Cloud Operations	SOC 2 (CC7.4); ISO 27001 (A.17.1); FedRAMP (CP-4)	Effective	
						
						
						
